## Usage

To use a specific source, configure ExternalDNS with the {{backtick 1}}--source{{backtick 1}} flag:

{{backtick 3}}bash
external-dns --source=service --source=ingress
{{backtick 3}}

Multiple sources can be combined to watch different resource types simultaneously.

To restrict sources to a subset of namespaces, see [Watching Multiple Namespaces](multiple-namespaces.md).

## Source Categories

- **Kubernetes Core**: Native Kubernetes resources (Service, Ingress, Pod, Node)
- **ExternalDNS**: Native ExternalDNS resources
- **Gateway API**: Kubernetes Gateway API resources (Gateway, HTTPRoute, etc.)
- **Service Mesh**: Service mesh implementations (Istio, Gloo)
- **Ingress Controllers**: Third-party ingress controller resources (Contour, Traefik, Ambassador, etc.)
- **Load Balancers**: Load balancer specific resources (F5)
- **OpenShift**: OpenShift specific resources (Route)
- **Cloud Platforms**: Cloud platform integrations (Cloud Foundry)
- **Wrappers**: Source wrappers that modify or combine other sources
- **Special**: Special purpose sources (connector, empty)
- **Testing**: Sources used for testing purposes

[^events-emit]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--events-emit{{backtick 1}} flag. Set to one or more of {{backtick 1}}RecordReady{{backtick 1}}, {{backtick 1}}RecordDeleted{{backtick 1}}, {{backtick 1}}RecordError{{backtick 1}} (repeat the flag for multiple). Defaults to none (events disabled).
[^filter-annotation]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--annotation-filter{{backtick 1}} flag. Filters resources queried for endpoints by annotation using label-selector semantics. Defaults to empty (no annotation filtering).
[^filter-label]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--label-filter{{backtick 1}} flag. Filters resources queried for endpoints by label selector. Defaults to empty (all resources).
[^namespace]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--namespace{{backtick 1}} flag. Accepts a single value to limit resources to one namespace. Defaults to empty (all namespaces).
[^namespaces]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--namespace{{backtick 1}} flag. Comma-separated or repeated to limit resources to specific namespaces. Defaults to empty (all namespaces).
[^fqdn-template]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--fqdn-template{{backtick 1}} flag. A templated string that generates DNS names for sources that don't define a hostname themselves. Repeat the flag for multiple templates. See [FQDN templating](../advanced/fqdn-templating.md).
[^val-annotation]: Controlled by the {{backtick 1}}--annotation-validation-mode{{backtick 1}} flag. Set to {{backtick 1}}warn{{backtick 1}} to log invalid or source-unsupported annotations, {{backtick 1}}strict{{backtick 1}} to additionally exclude affected objects from the informer index. Defaults to {{backtick 1}}off{{backtick 1}} (disabled).
[^val-spec]: Always on. Invalid endpoints are left out of the plan and reported in the object status. See [CRD validation](crd.md#validation).
